      "Universe each train day: the frozen universe rows (not excluded: no split window, no unexplained move) with prior close in the band, 14-day ATR (mean true range of the 14 daily bars before D, raw) \u003E= $0.50 and 20-day average volume \u003E= 1M shares. Bands: $5-$20 (the paper\u0027s \u003E $5 universe cut at the study\u0027s $20 ceiling) and $1-$5 (the same ATR and volume floors, so only the most volatile $1-$5 names qualify). Median names per day: $5-$20 163, $1-$5 13.",
      "",
      "Stocks in play: relative volume = the 09:30-09:35 volume (Alpaca SIP five-minute bar, raw) over its mean on the prior 14 sessions where the name had that bar (at least 10); ranked per day, at least 1.0x, top 10 / 20 / 50. The open bars were fetched for every universe name of the day and of the next 14 sessions (so a name\u0027s history exists before it enters), 769 day files (0 missing). A name without a bar in a history session is not counted there (a zero for an untraded or not-yet-listed session would inflate its relative volume).",
      "",
      "Trade (\u0060OpeningRangeBreakout\u0060, on the name\u0027s minute bars): side = the 09:30-09:35 candle (long if it closed above its open, short if below, a doji is skipped); entry = the open of the first real bar from 09:35 (within 5 minutes); stop = entry -/\u002B x ATR14 for x = 0.05 / 0.10 / 0.20 (the paper used 0.10), filled at the worse of the stop and the bar open, the entry bar\u0027s own range counting; else out at the 15:55 bar\u0027s open. Long only takes the up-candle names; short only the down-candle names; long \u002B short both. Minute bars: 51,381 symbol-days traded of 54,306 selected (4 without minute bars).",
      "",
      "Costs per round trip: (1) regular hours = Corwin-Schultz over the day\u0027s own 09:30-15:55 minute bars (a cost estimate only, no premarket multiplier; nothing selects on it) plus $0.0035/share each side; (2) the frozen model at $1,000 (that same spread x the premarket multiplier 9.393 from spread-multiplier.json, square-root impact on the 04:00-to-entry volume, 20-session sigma, floor 0.5 %); (3) commission only. Pooled = every train day (no model is fitted); per fold = the four half-year eval windows; day-clustered 95% bounds. Portfolio: the daily equal-weight return of the day\u0027s trades (cash on a day without one), annualized Sharpe (x sqrt 252), maximum drawdown of the compounded curve; and the paper\u0027s sizing (risk 1% of equity at the stop, at most 4x equity over N slots). DSR: per-trade deflated Sharpe of the regular-hours net at N = 5,519 (ledger total after this run), variance of this run\u0027s trial Sharpes 0.0013; frozen minimum 0.95. Finalist bar (explore-plan.md): \u003E= \u002B1.0% net per trade with lower bound \u003E 0, \u003E= 150 trades over \u003E= 40 days, \u003E 0 in at least 3 of 4 folds, leave-one-month-out lower bound \u003E 0, plus DSR \u003E= 0.95 (a per-trade bar: the ORB\u0027s edge, if any, is a few basis points per trade over many trades, so the Sharpe columns matter more here).",
